ailable options, price, and order data connected. Paste the full product URL rather than a shop homepage, search result, shortened social link, or image-only reference. After the information loads, compare it with the original marketplace page.\n\nOption labels may be unclear after translation. A listing can use picture numbers, package names, or internal codes. Match the option thumbnail, text, and price. If two variations are similar, add a short note such as “black, style B, size 42; do not substitute.”\n\nRecheck quantity and domestic freight. The headline price can represent the cheapest variation rather than the selected one, and the seller may charge delivery to the warehouse. Pause when the imported page and original listing disagree. An unexplained mismatch is a reason to verify, not a reason to click faster."
      ],
      [
        "Switch to DIY Order when automation loses the product",
        "Sugargoo’s official DIY Order guide presents it as a manual route for links the system cannot recognize or products from less common sources. It is useful when a short URL fails, the page requires login, the source is unsupported, or the seller has supplied a custom price. DIY Order is not a shortcut around missing information; it demands more detail because the platform cannot import the listing reliably.\n\nInclude the goods link when available, product name, store name, selected specifications, unit price, quantity, and domestic shipping fee. Upload an image showing the exact variation. Use remarks for operational facts: size, color, model number, engraving text, bundle contents, agreed price, or a request to confirm stock.\n\nWhen domestic shipping is unknown, label it unknown and ask the purchasing team to confirm it. A manual order should allow another person to identify the correct item without your browser history. If it cannot, the order is not ready."
      ],
      [
        "Separate must-confirm details from preferences",
        "A useful order note has priorities. Put outcome-changing details first: exact variation, quantity, compatibility, seller-supplied dimensions, included accessories, customization text, and whether substitution is allowed. Optional preferences, such as cleaner packaging or faster dispatch, come second.\n\nAn agent can relay a question but cannot force a seller to provide information, reserve stock, or guarantee quality. Avoid notes like “make sure it is perfect.” Replace them with checks that can be answered: “confirm the c